Package: unichef
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}
Description: cybersecurity and Unicode workbench for the terminal
 UniChef runs deterministic recipes of encoding, decoding, hashing,
 encryption, compression and text operations (Base64, hex, SHA-2,
 AES, JWT, gzip and more). It inspects text at the code-point level
 (names, blocks, scripts, Unicode properties, normalization and
 grapheme clusters) and detects invisible characters,
 bidirectional-control abuse (Trojan Source) and confusable homoglyphs.
 .
 Recipes are interchangeable with the UniChef web application and
 browser extensions.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-unichef
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, unichef (= ${binary:Version}), gnome-shell (>= 46)
Description: GNOME Shell extension for UniChef quick conversions
 Adds a UniChef icon to the GNOME top bar. Its popup runs any UniChef
 operation (Base64, hex, URL encoding, hashes and more) on typed or
 pasted text, and lists the code point, name and general category of
 each character, with buttons to copy the result.
 .
 It calls the unichef command on the local machine and makes no network
 requests. Enable it with:
 gnome-extensions enable unichef@0xdolan.github.io
